The third script (2result.sql) is the most accurate:

• It builds a per‑ball dataset first, so each delivery contributes only once to both runs and wickets, eliminating double‑counting.  
• Runs conceded include off‑the‑bat runs plus only those extras charged to the bowler (wides & no‑balls).  
• When counting wickets it excludes every dismissal type that is NOT credited to the bowler (‘run out’, ‘retired hurt’, ‘obstructing the field’), whereas 0result.sql counts them and 1result.sql removes only run‑outs.  
• Therefore its bowling‑average calculation is the closest to the Laws and usual score‑card practice.

```plaintext
2result.sql
```